      "latin": "recōgnitiō cōdicis",
      "status": "recommended",
      "period": "ours",
      "comment": "Our description: Traupman and Morgan–Owens have no word for a code review. <span lang=\"la\">Recōgnitiō</span> is a reviewing or examination (Col. 11.1.21; Suet. Claud. 16, in Lewis &amp; Short), and Egger’s word for going over what has been learned (M-O s.v. review); <span lang=\"la\">cōdicis</span> is the genitive of <span lang=\"la\">cōdex</span>, our word for code (see code).",
